# Inner loop write reaches the next outer iteration

Verifies an inner loop that rewrites an element is observed by the outer loop
on a later outer iteration. The outer body reads the element after the inner
loop, so both prints observe the stored `2cm` independently.

>>> source
let a: int[] = [10mm]

for (outer in 0..2) {
    for (inner in 0..1) {
        a[0] = 2cm
    }
    print(a[0])
}

<<< stdout
2cm
2cm

<<< stderr
